---
title: A delegated agent turn and a retained message (implemented)
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant RS as RunSupervisor
  participant L as AgentLauncher
  participant AS as AgentService
  participant X as NativeAgentTurnExecutor
  participant Store as WriteTransaction
  participant GW as Gateway (agents.* commands)
  participant Child as Child turn (AgentLauncher.launch_child)
  RS->>L: launch(root activation)
  L->>AS: materialize_primary (coordinator identity, session, assignment)
  L->>X: run(context, coordinator, stop)
  X->>Store: ControlService.begin_turn
  loop run_native_loop until no more tool calls
    X->>X: route context head, plan generation, provider request
    X->>GW: tool call agents.delegate (at most MAX_DELEGATE_CALLS_PER_TURN)
    GW->>AS: delegate(root, expected control revision, brief)
    AS->>Store: child agent, session, assignment and context (one write)
    X->>GW: tool call agents.post or agents.messages
    GW->>Store: message plus recipient delivery plus project event (one write)
  end
  X->>Store: ControlService.end_turn
  Note over L,Child: supervise_children polls every 500 ms, launches ready children up to max_subagents
  L->>Child: launch_child(assignment, activation, epoch)
  Child->>AS: activate_child
  Child->>X: run(child context)
  alt child finished
    Child->>AS: complete_child
  else it still has descendants
    Child->>AS: wait_for_descendants (assignment Waiting)
  end
  L->>AS: complete_primary only after every child is done
  Note over GW,Store: a recipient reads with agents.receive
  GW->>Store: deliver_inbox pass (commits delivery)
  Note right of GW: a wait repeats the pass, holding no write unit between polls
  GW->>Store: agents.ack Answered or Declined resolves the item
